`t ∈ [0, 1/200]` and `η ∈ [8, 17/2]`. The slab inputs and the two drift-block
Bernstein tables (at the error extremes `±3/200`) were generated by a numerical
search, are written as exact rationals and are not edited by hand. Each square
certificate is recomputed by `RationalLDL.propose` and checked by the kernel:
80 for the drift tables and 4 for the containment margin. Both tables are bound
to the slab's drift block by the exact rational polynomial test, and the metric
data is checked symmetric. `AIFCertifiedCell` assembles these into theorems. -/
